remarks:
Gravelly layer that can't be penetrated w/soil probe at 20 cm.; gravelly layer included a shell; hummocky surface (formed by Cx sterilis) w/Deschampsia & Andropogon on many hummocks. On toe of W-facing slope of large (Campbell) beach ridge. On mineral soil w/groundwater seepage. Typical of toe slopes of beach ridges. Water table presently well below ground surface.
3 corners were marked with spikes & 1 corner marked with a fork.
Coordinates of corners are:
47.66024_-96.41606;
47.66022_-96.41617;
47.66014_-96.41615;
47.66016_-96.41601.
